body:
### Description

Since commit `5cbd98a5be54` ("0029093: BOP PaveFiller hungs and constantly consumes memory", first released in 7.7.0), `BRepAlgoAPI_Fuse` of two swept tubes that meet at a shallow angle along a shared circle returns the two solids unmerged, still overlapping, with no error and no warning. 7.6.2 fuses the same input correctly.

We traced the commit itself, with and without the early
return (an environment switch added for the experiment):

Both lateral surfaces are periodic B-splines with the lens apex on their u
seams, so every start point exists twice, once per period. The cap circles
cross at two points, P56 and P44. The two seam crossings at the apex are
6.4e-3 mm apart. The section needs three curves: P56 to the apex, a short
bridge across the seam, and the apex to P44.

1. The walk from P56 ends where tube 2 sits on its cap boundary and tube 1 on
   its own. `ExtendLineInCommonZone` is entered there and the new check fires.
   Without it the call appends one point 3e-6 mm from the corner. The same
   happens twice at P44.
2. `IntPatch_PrmPrmIntersection` first walks the bridge itself: three points,
   identical in both runs.
3. A second pass walks the last sampled seed again, which is the bridge end in
   the other period. With the early return bypassed that walk returns one point
   and the line is dropped. With the early return active it returns three
   points. `IntWalk_PWalking` is one object reused across seeds, so state left
   by the skipped extension probably explains the difference. We did not find
   which state.
4. `DublicateOfLinesProcessing` keeps the line with more points. The new
   candidate has four points and the bridge found first has three, so the
   bridge is removed. The candidate sits one period away from the face domain
   on both surfaces.
5. `IntTools_LineConstructor` returns no parts for it. No curve crosses the
   seam, two vertices stay open, and the classification keeps the lens pieces
   inside the other solid.

The early return is not wrong for a line that runs along a bound; that is the
case the commit message describes and the extension is wasted there. The check
tests only the last point, so it cannot tell that case from a line that ends on
a bound, which is what the line from P56 does. The test added with the commit
is a performance test (`tests/perf/modalg/bug29093`) and does not check that a
closed section survives.

### Illustration

The same construction (wire radius 6 on a helix of radius 50) rendered from the side, cropped to the joint. The renders come from an application built on OCCT 7.6.2, using two radii where the fuse succeeds and fails; the failing fuse on 7.7 and later has the same topology as the right-hand image.

The two operands, coloured separately: the caps share a centre and cross along a diameter, so tube 1 (blue) and tube 2 (orange) overlap in a thin wedge on one side (blue showing through orange at the top) and leave a gap on the other (dark wedge at the bottom).

<img width="440" alt="The two operands: overlap wedge at the top, gap wedge at the bottom" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fab6c84d-7fbc-46fa-ab1d-9d88d47ed649" />

The fused result in x-ray view. Left: the fuse merged the tubes; above the crest only one edge remains where the overlap was removed, and below it the two edges of the gap open apart. Right: the fuse failed; both end caps are still present and cross each other, so the two solids overlap.

<img width="360" alt="Fuse merged: one edge above the crest" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/584b5df3-3501-4496-9559-84dc2f269588" /> <img width="360" alt="Fuse failed: both end caps remain and cross" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/44353ace-8245-42f8-8906-81a7c26f655f" />

### Bisect

`git bisect` over the 293 commits between `V7_6_2` and `V7_7_0`, on the test
above (good means one solid and an overlap within 0.5 to 1.5 of the predicted
wedge), ends at `5cbd98a5be54`. Its parent `25b5e83a4c8c` is good. No commit in
the range failed to build. The full bisect log is available on request.

### Wider evidence

- 192 nudged variants of the joint (relative changes of R and r): 7.6.2 fails 8; 7.7.2, 7.8.1, 7.9.3 and 8.0.1 fail all 192; 8.0.1 with the patch below fails 7, all among the 8 that already fail on 7.6.2 (a second, older defect not addressed here).
- Two tilted helical caps at 5.72 degrees, 12 variants: 7.6.2 fails 1, 8.0.1 fails 12, patched 8.0.1 fails 1.

### Candidate patch

The early return in `IntWalk_PWalking::ExtendLineInCommonZone` tests only whether the last point lies within the parametric resolution of a bound, so it also matches a line that merely ends on a bound. The patch narrows it to a line that runs along a bound (the last point and the one before it on the same bound), the case the 0029093 commit message describes. It is a heuristic; a maintainer may prefer a direction test.

**Not yet run against the DRAW test suite**, including `tests/perf/modalg/bug29093`, so whether the original hang stays fixed is untested. We will add those results here; a pull request can follow.

```diff
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/IntWalk/IntWalk_PWalking.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/IntWalk/IntWalk_PWalking.cxx
index eef4634dd..88f880338 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/IntWalk/IntWalk_PWalking.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKGeomAlgo/IntWalk/IntWalk_PWalking.cxx
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include <IntSurf_PntOn2S.hxx>
 #include <IntWalk_PWalking.hxx>
 #include <IntWalk_StatusDeflection.hxx>
+#include <cmath>
 #include <math_FunctionSetRoot.hxx>
 #include <Precision.hxx>
 #include <Standard_Failure.hxx>
@@ -1858,38 +1859,48 @@ bool IntWalk_PWalking::ExtendLineInCommonZone(const IntImp_ConstIsoparametric th

   previousPoint.Parameters(Param(1), Param(2), Param(3), Param(4));

-  if (Param(1) - UFirst1 < ResoU1)
-  {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
-  }
-  else if (Param(2) - VFirst1 < ResoV1)
-  {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
-  }
-  else if (Param(3) - UFirst2 < ResoU2)
-  {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
-  }
-  else if (Param(4) - VFirst2 < ResoV2)
-  {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
-  }
+  const double aLow[4]  = {UFirst1, VFirst1, UFirst2, VFirst2};
+  const double aHigh[4] = {ULast1, VLast1, ULast2, VLast2};
+  const double aReso[4] = {ResoU1, ResoV1, ResoU2, ResoV2};

-  if (Param(1) - ULast1 > -ResoU1)
-  {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
-  }
-  else if (Param(2) - VLast1 > -ResoV1)
-  {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
-  }
-  else if (Param(3) - ULast2 > -ResoU2)
-  {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
-  }
-  else if (Param(4) - VLast2 > -ResoV2)
+  // Bit i is set when parameter i lies within its resolution of the lower bound,
+  // bit i + 4 when it lies within its resolution of the upper bound.
+  auto aBoundMask = [&](const double theParam[4]) {
+    int aMask = 0;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
+    {
+      if (theParam[i] - aLow[i] < aReso[i])
+      {
+        aMask |= (1 << i);
+      }
+      if (theParam[i] - aHigh[i] > -aReso[i])
+      {
+        aMask |= (1 << (i + 4));
+      }
+    }
+    return aMask;
+  };
+
+  // A line that merely ends on a parametric bound must still be extended: the
+  // extension is what bridges two half curves that stop short of a shared crest.
+  // Only a line that runs along the bound has nothing left to extend.
+  const int aLastMask = aBoundMask(&Param(1));
+  if (aLastMask != 0 && line->NbPoints() >= 2)
   {
-    return bOutOfTangentZone;
+    double aLastLine[4];
+    line->Value(line->NbPoints()).Parameters(aLastLine[0], aLastLine[1], aLastLine[2], aLastLine[3]);
+    bool aLastIsPrevious = true;
+    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)
+    {
+      aLastIsPrevious = aLastIsPrevious && std::abs(aLastLine[i] - Param(i + 1)) < 1.e-12;
+    }
+    const int aBeforeIndex = aLastIsPrevious ? line->NbPoints() - 1 : line->NbPoints();
+    double    aBefore[4];
+    line->Value(aBeforeIndex).Parameters(aBefore[0], aBefore[1], aBefore[2], aBefore[3]);
+    if ((aBoundMask(aBefore) & aLastMask) != 0)
+    {
+      return bOutOfTangentZone;
+    }
   }

   while (!bStop)
```

### Expected Behavior

One solid, with the 14.398 mm3 overlap wedge between the tubes removed, as on 7.6.2.

### Actual Behavior

| OCCT | Solids | Overlap removed (mm3) | Expected |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 7.6.2 | 1 | 14.398226 | 14.398121 |
| 8.0.1 | 2 | 0.000100 | 14.398121 |
| 8.0.1 with the candidate patch | 1 | 14.398227 | 14.398121 |

The two solids overlap. `BRepAlgoAPI_Fuse` reports no error and no warning.

### Sample Code

```cpp
// Minimal reproduction for the upstream report. Two helical tubes meet end to
// end; their end caps cross along a diameter and the tube surfaces meet at a
// dihedral angle of 5.72 degrees along the cap circles. The fuse must remove a
// wedge of 14.398 mm3 (the lens where tube 1 and tube 2 overlap). Only OCCT is
// used.
//
//   g++ -O2 -std=c++17 -I<occt>/include/opencascade bridge-min.cpp -o bridge-min \
//     -L<occt>/lib -lTKernel -lTKMath -lTKG2d -lTKG3d -lTKGeomBase -lTKBRep \
//     -lTKGeomAlgo -lTKTopAlgo -lTKPrim -lTKBO -lTKBool -lTKShHealing -lTKOffset
//
// Output: solid count of the fuse and the volume it removed. A closed section
// gives 1 solid and 14.398. An open section gives 2 solids and about 0.
#include <BRepAlgoAPI_Fuse.hxx>
#include <BRepBuilderAPI_MakeEdge.hxx>
#include <BRepBuilderAPI_MakeWire.hxx>
#include <BRepGProp.hxx>
#include <BRepLib.hxx>
#include <BRepOffsetAPI_MakePipeShell.hxx>
#include <GProp_GProps.hxx>
#include <Geom2d_Line.hxx>
#include <Geom_CylindricalSurface.hxx>
#include <Standard_Failure.hxx>
#include <TopExp.hxx>
#include <TopTools_IndexedMapOfShape.hxx>
#include <TopoDS_Edge.hxx>
#include <TopoDS_Shape.hxx>
#include <TopoDS_Wire.hxx>
#include <gp_Ax2.hxx>
#include <gp_Ax3.hxx>
#include <gp_Circ.hxx>
#include <gp_Dir.hxx>
#include <gp_Dir2d.hxx>
#include <gp_Pnt.hxx>
#include <gp_Pnt2d.hxx>

#include <cmath>
#include <cstdio>

namespace {

const double kPi = 3.14159265358979323846;
const double kDeg = kPi / 180.0;
const double kRadius = 50.0;
const double kTube = 6.0;
const double kAngle1 = 2.278524728621996;
const double kTheta = 5.724061592216415;

TopoDS_Shape helixTube(const gp_Pnt& origin, double pitch, int turns) {
  const gp_Ax3 axis(origin, gp_Dir(0, 0, 1));
  Handle(Geom_Surface) surface = new Geom_CylindricalSurface(axis, kRadius);
  Handle(Geom2d_Curve) line = new Geom2d_Line(gp_Pnt2d(0, 0), gp_Dir2d(2 * kPi, pitch));
  const double length = std::sqrt(4 * kPi * kPi + pitch * pitch);
  TopoDS_Edge edge = BRepBuilderAPI_MakeEdge(line, surface, 0, turns * length).Edge();
  BRepLib::BuildCurve3d(edge, 1e-7, GeomAbs_C1, 14, 200);

  const gp_Pnt start(origin.X() + kRadius, origin.Y(), origin.Z());
  const gp_Dir tangent(0, 2 * kPi * kRadius, pitch);
  const gp_Circ circle(gp_Ax2(start, tangent), kTube);
  TopoDS_Wire profile = BRepBuilderAPI_MakeWire(BRepBuilderAPI_MakeEdge(circle).Edge()).Wire();
  TopoDS_Wire spine = BRepBuilderAPI_MakeWire(edge).Wire();

  BRepOffsetAPI_MakePipeShell sweep(spine);
  sweep.SetMode(Standard_True);
  sweep.SetTolerance(1e-5, 1e-5, 1e-2);
  sweep.Add(profile, TopExp::FirstVertex(edge, Standard_True), Standard_False, Standard_False);
  sweep.Build();
  if (!sweep.IsDone() || !sweep.MakeSolid()) {
    throw Standard_Failure("sweep failed");
  }
  return sweep.Shape();
}

double volume(const TopoDS_Shape& shape) {
  GProp_GProps props;
  BRepGProp::VolumeProperties(shape, props, 1e-6, false, true);
  return props.Mass();
}

int countSolids(const TopoDS_Shape& shape) {
  TopTools_IndexedMapOfShape solids;
  TopExp::MapShapes(shape, TopAbs_SOLID, solids);
  return solids.Extent();
}

}  // namespace

int main() {
  const double pitch1 = 2 * kPi * kRadius * std::tan(kAngle1 * kDeg);
  const double pitch2 = 2 * kPi * kRadius * std::tan((kAngle1 + kTheta) * kDeg);
  const TopoDS_Shape a = helixTube(gp_Pnt(0, 0, 0), pitch1, 1);
  const TopoDS_Shape b = helixTube(gp_Pnt(0, 0, pitch1), pitch2, 6);
  BRepAlgoAPI_Fuse fuse(a, b);
  if (!fuse.IsDone() || fuse.HasErrors()) {
    std::printf("fuse failed\n");
    return 1;
  }
  const double removed = volume(a) + volume(b) - volume(fuse.Shape());
  std::printf("solids=%d overlapRemoved=%.6f expected=14.398121\n", countSolids(fuse.Shape()), removed);
  return 0;
}
```

### Environment

- Operating system: Linux (Debian 13, aarch64)
- Compiler: GCC 14.2
- Bitness: 64-bit
- OCCT version: latest (8.0.1); also 7.7.0, 7.7.2, 7.8.1, 7.9.3. Correct on 7.6.2.
